 * consumer precisely what `@mkbabb/glass-ui/styles/fonts` delivers — no
 * third-party CDN, no off-canon families, and no typography preset: the demo
 * renders the library default with zero override.
 *
 * The published `src/styles/fonts.css` `@font-face` rules reference the
 * woff2 via the `url("@mkbabb/glass-ui/fonts/…")` package-specifier shape
 * that the publish-time `publishStyleAssets` plugin base64-inlines at
 * library build. That bare-specifier `url()` does NOT resolve in the
 * demo's Vite dev/preview context (Vite's CSS pipeline doesn't resolve
 * bare specifiers in `url()` — the very Option-A blocker documented in
 * vite.config.ts). So the demo re-declares the SAME faces (identical
 * family names, weight axes, unicode-range subsetting, and font-display
 * registers as fonts.css) but points at the source woff2 by a demo-
 * resolvable relative path — `../src/fonts/<family>/<face>.woff2`. These
 * are the SAME binaries the publish step inlines, so the demo renders the
 * published corpus byte-for-byte. The relative-path declaration lives in
